# Module pattern

Each module in `apps/web/src/modules/<name>/`:

```
<name>/
├── shared.tsx              # columns, formFields, defaults, header action, status maps
├── <Name>sListPage.tsx     # CrudMainView only — no custom table UI
├── <Name>CreatePage.tsx    # ModulePage + EntityForm
└── <Name>DetailPage.tsx     # ModulePage + DetailView OR Tabs
```

## shared.tsx owns config

- `*PageIcon()` — re-export from `@/lib/modulePageIcons` (or `userRecordPageIcon` for user detail). Pass to every `CrudMainView` / `ModulePage` in the module.
- `*Columns: CrudColumn[]` — column defs, `variantMap` in `meta` for status columns
- `*FormFields: FormField[]` + `*FormDefaults` + exported value type
- `*HeaderAction` — returns `<PageHeaderCtaLink>` with icon + “New …”
- Status maps (`CLIENT_STATUS_MAP`) — reuse in columns, detail subtitle, and DetailView fields

## List page

- Use `useListPageState()` from `@/lib/useListPageState` — do not hand-roll search/filter/sort/page state
- Pass returned props to `CrudMainView`: `entityLabel`, `getRowHref`, `exportOptions`, `headerActions`

```tsx
<CrudMainView
  title="Clients"
  icon={clientsPageIcon()}
  headerActions={<ClientsHeaderAction />}
  columns={clientColumns}
  entityLabel="client"
  getRowHref={(c) => `/clients/${c.id}`}
  exportOptions={{ fileName: 'clients' }}
  …
/>
```

## Don't

- Column or form field defs inline in page files — belongs in `shared.tsx`
- Custom list layouts bypassing `CrudMainView`
- `ModulePage` / `CrudMainView` without `icon` prop
- Per-module export wiring — use `exportOptions` on `CrudMainView`
